---
// The Chinese serif (Noto Serif SC, from our own site since 2026-10-09:
// src/lib/notes.ts CJK_SERIF_CSS) for a page with Chinese on it, linked so
// that it never holds the first paint.
//
// The stylesheet is only @font-face rules: ~100 KB compressed (410 KB of
// CSS once unpacked, every unicode-range slice of four weights), and as a
// plain render-blocking <link> the page waited for all of it before
// painting a word — on a phone's network, and from where Google was slow,
// that is the whole wait. Its faces are `display=swap`, so what the reader
// sees is unchanged: the Chinese is set in the system face first and in
// the serif once its slices arrive, exactly as before; only the page is
// there sooner. On a full load it waits as print media and is switched to
// all once it has arrived; without script, the <noscript> link. An in-site
// arrival is as before: the router has loaded the sheet before the swap,
// and Layout's before-swap listener sets it to all on the incoming page
// (data-swap-media), so it applies from the arrival's first frame (and the
// swap keeps a link already on the page, Astro's persistedHeadElement).
import { CJK_SERIF_CSS } from '../../lib/notes';
---

<link rel="preload" as="style" href={CJK_SERIF_CSS} />
<link rel="stylesheet" href={CJK_SERIF_CSS} media="print" onload="this.media='all'" data-swap-media />
<noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href={CJK_SERIF_CSS} /></noscript>
